  "reason": "Evidence: config_042 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieved the best accuracy at 0.7250, with config_013 (same but concat) close behind at 0.7207. The scvi_n200 RNA encoder is clearly the dominant factor (~20% gap over scgpt). Uncertainty: we have not yet tested whether the image encoder choice (imagenet_vit_l vs resnet50) meaningfully affects performance when paired with the strong scvi_n200 encoder. This experiment (config_049: scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) is a clean single-variable ablation of the best config, changing only the image encoder. If resnet50 performs comparably, it confirms the RNA encoder dominates and frees us to explore other levers; if it underperforms, it confirms imagenet_vit_l is critical and we should focus remaining budget on refining around that backbone. With 4 experiments left, this targeted test maximally reduces uncertainty about the most impactful remaining design choice while staying in the high-performing region."
}

